Package: mkdraw
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/mythicalkingdom/mkbbs
Description: ANSI screen editor and CP437 viewer for BBS screens
 mkdraw is a text mode editor for the 80 x 23 screens that bulletin board
 systems show to their callers: ANSI art, AVATAR, plain ASCII and the Pascal
 source that writes a screen.  Every cell is one IBM PC (CP437) character with
 a colour attribute, as on a DOS machine; a UTF-8 terminal shows the Unicode
 equivalents.  It has the box drawing sets, area commands, and a list of BBS
 screen codes.
 .
 mkcat shows such a file (a screen, a message, a DOS log) on a terminal of
 today: it turns the CP437 characters into UTF-8, or leaves them for a BBS
 terminal such as SyncTERM, and keeps the colours of the art as drawn.
 .
 Both are part of the MK BBS (package mkbbs, which includes them); they need
 no BBS to run.
